From 8807a39f7d8037bdd781fd8d22dd5084b8dfe045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <info@fvanmaele.de>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:50:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] [clangd] workspace/symbol: template arguments never
 searched, operators kept, tiers in score

With middleMatch the fuzzy score was computed on the whole name, so
EBOBaseImpl<T, true, CtorNotOnDevice> still matched "ector" through E +
Ctor inside its template arguments, although patch 0012 says arguments are
not searched. Both the fuzzy and the contiguous match now run on the name
without template arguments (workspaceSymbolMatch, one rule for Dex,
MemIndex and getWorkspaceSymbols, which each had a copy). An operator's
`<` is its name: "operator<<" was cut to "operator".

The exposed score of a second-tier match is mapped like the ranking score,
so a client that sorts by it keeps the tiers. looseScope and middleMatch
accept null as "not given"; a middleMatch of 1, 2 or below 0 is an
InvalidParams error, no longer raised to 3 silently.
